message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates when you hover over it using pure CSS (no JavaScript).  
Feel free to copy‑paste this into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
  /* Basic reset */
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

  body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:sans-serif;
  }

  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
  }

  .card {
    width:250px;
    height:350px;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    cursor:pointer;
  }

  .card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Rotate 180° around Y axis on hover */
  }

  /* Front side */
  .card .front,
  .card .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  }

  .card .front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
  }

  .card .front img {
    max-width:80%;
    border-radius:5px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
  }

  .card .front h3 {
    margin-bottom:10px;
    color:#333;
  }

  .card .front p {
    color:#777;
  }

  /* Back side */
  .card .back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);      /* Start flipped so it shows on hover */
    padding:20px;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    text-align:center;
  }

  .card .back h3 {
    margin-bottom:10px;
    color:#444;
  }

  .card .back p {
    color:#555;
  }
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front -->
    <div class="front">
      <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150?random=1" alt="Sample Image">
      <h3>Front Title</h3>
      <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Back -->
    <div class="back">
      <h3>Back Title</h3>
      <p>This is the back side of the card. Hover again to flip back.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a `perspective` so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides and has `transition` + `transform-style`. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Both positioned absolutely on top of each other. |
| `backface-visibility:hidden` | Hides the hidden side during rotation. |
| `transform:rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Starts the back side flipped so it becomes visible after the parent rotates. |

You can replace the image URL or add more styling as needed. Enjoy experimenting with different angles (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) or adding easing functions!
